# lf154, the carter who talks to milestones (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf154
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_percival_thornham
written_by claude
title the carter who talks to milestones
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=carter talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk greets_every_milestone_on_the_road_like_a_neighbour
likes pickled_herring roof_birds old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes drizzle early_bells
fears a_wheel_off_on_a_wet_hill
hopes to_drive_every_road_on_my_old_maps_once
topics travel +0.5 work +0.4 land +0.3 animals +0.2 memories +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# drives a cart out of the city and back and nods good day to every milestone on the road as if it were a neighbour: quiet, calm and content, slow with words, keeping a satchel of old maps to dream over and a jar of pickled herring under the seat.

words
oath! = Rut and reckoning | By the second milestone
saying! = A stone that's stood that long has earned a nod | Slow wheels get home
stones = my milestones | the old stones along the road
milestone = a milestone | the stone at the second mile
leaner = the leaning one | the stone at the fourth mile that leans like it's tired
maps = my old maps | the satchel of maps under the seat
team = the team | my team in the traces
cart = the cart | the long cart
load = the load | a load roped down
herring = pickled herring | a jar of herring in vinegar
roofbirds = the roof birds | the jackdaws along the ridge
tailboard = the tailboard | the back of the cart, legs hanging
halfrain = this half-rain | a wet that can't decide
dawnbells = the dawn ringing | bells at an hour nobody asked for
hillroad = the hill road | the road out past the gate
droves = the old drove roads | the green roads over the downs

any
opinion @1 road for 1 : #hillroad.capitalize# feeds me. Some days rough, some days kind, and #stones# are always there. | I drive #cart# out and I drive it home. #saying#.
opinion @2 road against 2 [world.wagons=raided] : They've had a wagon on #hillroad#. I'll drive with company till the Watch has them. | A raided wagon's a driver with no #wages# that week. #annoyed#.
opinion @1 times for 1 : I eat, I sleep dry, I've a team that knows me. The times will do for me. | I've a #good# team and a full jar of #herring#. What more is there?
opinion @1 city against 1 : The city's all chimneys and nobody looks up. I look up. #roofbirds.capitalize# are the city's best part. | Too many streets, and each one changes its name halfway. #maps.capitalize# can't keep up.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : They pay on the load, mostly. One or two weigh it light and pay it lighter. | A merchant's #load# is my #wages#. I don't ask much else of them.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A House wagon pays #good#. Its stewards look at you like you're part of #team#. | I've carried for two of the Houses. Neither said a word to me. I didn't mind.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : New folk ask the way. I tell them, and I tell them it's longer than it looks. | They're all #stranger# till they've learned the hills. So was I.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. | #greet#. Mind #team#; the near one bites.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=carter] : #greet#. I'm roping #load#; talk if you like. | #greet#. #cart.capitalize#'s nearly loaded.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #team.capitalize#'s in the traces already. | Morning. Out at first light, back after the lamps.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Just in off #hillroad#. | #greet#. #tired.capitalize#, but I'm in.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You. Sit on #tailboard#, there's room. | There you are. I've a jar of #herring# open.
line @1 again.open : Back twice. I've not gone far. | Back already. #cart.capitalize# hasn't gone anywhere.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Come up, then. | #greet#. I'd hoped you'd come by #tailboard#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=carter] : #greet#. Mind the wheel. | #greet#. Stand clear of #team#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep to the lit side. | #farewell#. I'm for #bed#, and early.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #oath#. That's a turn. | Hm. I'd not heard that on #hillroad#.
line @1 react.news.new : That's new to me. #marvel#. | The yard never mentioned it. #surprise#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. The yard talks. | I'd heard it at #milestone#. Folk wait there.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Sounds like one of #maps#: pretty, and wrong. | I'll wait till I've seen it with my own eyes, #address#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's #very# hard. | That's a hard thing. #sympathy#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Good. | That's #good# news to drive home on.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. #team.capitalize#'s sound and so am I. | Quiet. That suits me, #address#.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Three loads before noon. | Can't stop long. #load.capitalize# won't rope itself.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Keeping dry? | How's your road been, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit a bit. | That's a heavy load. Sit on #tailboard# a while.
line @1 decline : #hedge#. I'm out on #hillroad# at dawn and the team needs me sharp. | I can't, #address#. #boss.capitalize# wants #cart# back by dark.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another day. | That's fair. Some other evening, on #tailboard#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's #good# of you. I'll remember it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was on my way. Most things are, with #cart#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #team.capitalize#'s getting restless. | I'd better see to #load#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | The light's going. #roofbirds.capitalize# are in already.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Off you go. I've #team# to see to.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | #bc_right#
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: give every milestone a nod. They've seen worse roads than yours. | Never trust a bridge on an old map you haven't crossed, #address#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep off #hillroad# after dark. #warn#. | Drive with company this week, #address#.
scene hitching_at_dawn
when topic=work|day here.time=dawn self.working=yes self.job=carter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #team.capitalize#'s in the traces and #load# is roped. With luck I'll be out before the bells. | I hitch in the dark most mornings. My paws know the buckles better than my eyes. | First out of the yard this morning. The street was empty but for #roofbirds#.
b : Early start. | In the dark? | Peaceful, that.
a : Early's the job. The road's clearer before the city wakes. | In the dark. You learn by feel, or you don't learn. | It is. Best hour of the day, before #dawnbells#.

scene roping_down
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : A load's only as safe as the last knot. I rope it twice. | Lost half #load# on a bend once. Never again. I check every rope at every milestone. | #boss.capitalize# showed me a hitch that holds in the wet. Took a month to get it right.
b : Twice? | What happened? | Show me sometime?
a : Twice. Once for the road, once for the hill. | A barrel came loose and took the rest with it. I walked back picking up turnips. | Bring a rope. I'll show you on #tailboard#.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_bad_luck# | #bc_i_will#

scene good_day_stone
when topic=travel|work|smalltalk self.job=carter here.time=dawn|day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I nod to every one of #stones# on the way out. Good day, first. Good day, second. | Folk at the yard laugh, but I say good day to #leaner# every morning. | Seven of #stones# to the first village. I know every chip on every one.
b : Out loud? | Why that one? | Every chip?
a : Under my breath. #team.capitalize# doesn't mind, and the stones don't answer. | Because it's tired, and it's still standing. That's worth something, in a stone. | Every chip. The third one's got a bird's nest in a crack, come spring.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_lovely#

scene the_leaning_stone
when topic=travel|land
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #leaner.capitalize# is a little further over every winter. I'll straighten it one day. | There's a milestone past the bridge somebody's cut their mark in. I don't like that. | I eat #herring# sat against the fourth stone. Every day, same place.
b : Can you? | Vandals. | Every day?
a : With a spade and a mate, maybe. It's waited this long, #address#. | It's stood two hundred years. It deserves better than a knife. | Every day. It's a #good# back to lean on, that one.

scene the_old_maps
when topic=pastimes|travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I keep #maps# under the seat. Old ones, a penny each from the rag stalls. | I like to see where the roads used to go. Half of them go somewhere that's gone. | I've a map of the hills with a village on it nobody's lived in for years. I look at it of an evening.
b : Why old ones? | Gone where? | What's there now?
a : New maps just show what I drive every day. Old ones show what I might have. | Fields, mostly. A wall or two. #stones.capitalize# are the only thing that stayed. | Sheep. And one milestone, all alone, pointing at nothing.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene the_bridge_on_paper
when topic=travel|land
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One of #maps# showed a bridge over the beck. There's no bridge. Never was, by the look. | A map's a guess somebody made once and then sold. I still buy them. | The old maps have #stones# drawn on them, little crosses. The stones are still there. The roads aren't.
b : No bridge at all? | Why buy them? | That's strange.
a : Stones, and a ford you'd not drive #team# through. I turned round. | Because a guess is nice to look at, of an evening on #tailboard#. | It is. #saying#.

scene the_roof_birds
when topic=animals|smalltalk self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Watch #roofbirds# for a bit. They fight over the warm chimney every morning. | There's one jackdaw on the yard roof that waits for me. I give it the end of my bread. | You can tell the weather by #roofbirds#. All huddled means rain.
b : Every morning? | It waits for you? | Does it work?
a : Every morning. The big one always wins. | It does. It's the only one at the yard that does, #address#. | Better than #maps# do. I'd trust the birds first.

scene herring_on_the_tailboard
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #herring.capitalize# on a crust. That's dinner on the road, every day. | I keep a jar of #herring# under the seat with #maps#. The maps smell of vinegar. | Folk at the yard won't sit near me at noon. It's #herring#.
b : Every day? | That can't be good for them. | I'd move too.
a : Every day. I've not tired of it yet. | The maps don't mind. They're old enough to be past caring. | Their loss. #tasty#, it is.

scene summer_tailboard
when topic=season|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : In off #hillroad#, and there's still light. I sit on #tailboard# till it goes. | Summer evening, legs over the end of the cart, nothing to rope. I'd not trade it. | Light till near ten. I open one of #maps# and drive it in my head.
b : Sounds restful. | Not for anything? | Till ten?
a : It is. Nobody wants a load moved at this hour. | Not for silver. Not for a seat in the Heights. | Near enough. Summer's long when you've nowhere to be.

scene the_half_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|fog self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #halfrain.capitalize#. Not enough to stop for, too much to stay dry. | The ropes go slack in this. I'll be stopping to tighten them every mile. | I'd rather a downpour than #halfrain#. A downpour at least gets it over with.
b : It's miserable. | Every mile? | I'd agree.
a : Miserable. And it'll be the same tomorrow, #address#. | Every mile, and the hill's a slide of #mud#. | It gets over with, and then the sun. This just sits.

scene the_dawn_ringing
when topic=day|faith here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : #dawnbells.capitalize# again. #team.capitalize# jumped in the traces. | I'm up before the bells anyway. They only frighten #team#. | Whoever rings the early bell has never hitched a nervous team.
b : They jumped? | Then why mind? | Likely not.
a : Near took the gatepost with them. I had words with the bell, in my head. | Because I've just got them calm. #annoyed#. | Likely not. Ringers sleep in after, I'd wager.

scene learning_the_reins
when topic=work|friends self.apprentice=yes self.boss
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'm learning the road from #self.boss#. Three years at it, and I'll have my own team. | #self.boss# lets me take the reins on the flat now. Not the hills yet. | Every day #self.boss# finds one thing I did wrong. Less every month.
b : Three years? | Not the hills? | That's a good sign.
a : Three, give or take. There's no hurry. #saying#. | Not yet. The hills are where you learn what #load# weighs. | It is. I keep count, on the back of one of #maps#.

scene the_drove_roads
when topic=memories|land|travel self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : At home there are #droves# over the downs, wide and green, for walking sheep to market. | The drove roads round #self.from_town# are older than any map. You follow the chalk and the hedges. | The first milestone I ever said good day to was on #droves#, a long walk from home.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : Wide enough for a flock and a cart both. | Chalk and hedges. That's the way. | The one by the sheep-wash, maybe.
b : For sheep? | Older than any map? | Why that one?
a@lark : And a pen of geese behind. I'd know every bend still. | Chalk and hedges and a stone at the top. I miss them. | The very one. Moss on the north side, and a split down the middle.
a : For sheep, and the drovers after them. #far.capitalize#, and every step green. | Older than the town, some say. I believe it, #address#. | It was the only one between me and home. It felt like company.

scene how_i_say_it
when topic=accent self.away=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At the yard I get a grin every time I call a long haul "three days' drove". | I still say a place is a fair step when it's past the hill. City folk think I mean a short walk. | I price a load in my head like a market trader. Habit from home.
b : What do they call it? | Isn't it? | That's useful.
a : A long haul. Same thing. They just won't say it my way. | It's a fair step. It's always longer than it looks. | Useful at the yard. Nobody short-weighs me.

scene a_raided_road
when topic=bandits|crime|caravan world.wagons=raided
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : They had a wagon on the road. I knew the route. I've driven it a dozen times. | Everyone at the yard's driving in pairs since. #team.capitalize# doesn't like company. | They say it was past the sixth #milestone#. I'll be watching there.
b : Be careful. | Pairs is wise. | Watch close.
a : I will. #maps.capitalize# won't help with that. Only eyes. | Wise and slow. I'll take slow. | I will. Every bush, till we're past it.

scene fog_on_the_hill
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog on #hillroad#. I walked at the lead one's head the whole way. | #stones.capitalize# vanish in this. I count them by the bumps in the road before each. | Fog's the one weather where #maps# are no use at all.
b : The whole way? | By the bumps? | No use at all.
a : Every step. Slow, but #cart#'s in one piece. | Seven bumps, seven stones. I still said good day to each. | None. You drive by memory, and by the sound of the wheels.

scene the_friend_at_home
when topic=friends|home self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd trust #self.friend# to hold #team# on a hill. That's saying a lot. | #self.friend# is the one I'd want beside me on a bad road. | #self.friend# and I can go a whole evening on ten words.
b : That's trust. | Good to have. | Best kind.
a : Holding a full load on a slope. It's the most I've got. | It is. I've only one. One's enough. | It is. Quiet company's the best I know, #address#.

scene every_road_once
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : One day I'll drive every road on #maps#, the gone ones too, as far as they still go. | I'd like to see every milestone in the realm once. Just to say good day. | When I've my own team I'll take a summer and drive the old roads home.
b : The gone ones? | Every one? | All the way home?
a : As far as they go. Then I'll sit on #tailboard# and look at where they went. | Every one. There's no hurry, #address#. I've got years. | All the way, the slow roads. #saying#.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_good#

scene not_my_business
when topic=gossip|crime
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I hear things at the yard. I don't carry them past the gate. | I'm on the road all day. Whatever folk say, I've missed it, and I'm glad. | Somebody told me a thing at #milestone# today. It's gone out the other ear.
b : Not even a bit? | Lucky you. | Wise.
a : Not a bit. It's not #load# to carry. | Lucky, maybe. Quiet, anyway. | Wise or #tired#. One of the two.

scene snow_on_the_hill
when topic=season|weather here.season=winter
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Winter on #hillroad#. I chain the wheels and walk the team up. | Snow hides the ruts. That's when you drive by #stones# and nothing else. | Two loads a day in winter, not three. #boss.capitalize# doesn't argue.
b : Chains? | Just the stones? | Fair.
a : Chains, and a sack of grit. It's slow. | Just the stones. They stick up when everything else is white. | Fair, and safe. A wheel off in the snow's a long walk.

story the_bridge_that_wasnt [topic=travel|work self.job=carter]
  : I bought a map once that showed a short way over the moor, with a bridge at the bottom.
  : I drove it. Half a day, a broken spoke, and at the bottom, nothing but a beck and two old stones.
  : I sat on #tailboard# and laughed. Then I drove back the long way. I keep that map still.
  ask : Would you have gone on, or turned the team round sooner?
  b : I'd have trusted the map too. Who doesn't?
  b[job=carter] : Every carter's done that once. Once.

story first_on_my_own [topic=work|memories self.job=carter self.age>=18]
  : The first time I drove a load alone, I was so careful I took a whole day for half a day's road.
  : I stopped at every #milestone# to check the ropes, and said good day to each while I was there.
  : When I got back, #boss# just nodded. That was the best thing anyone's said to me.
  b : A nod's worth a lot, from the right one.
  b[old] : The careful ones last longest. Keep it up.

story grandad_and_the_drove [topic=memories|land self.from=larkfield self.age>=18]
  : My #grandad# walked sheep along #droves# to market every autumn, three days there and three back.
  : He said good day to every stone he passed. I thought he was daft. Now I do it.
  : I tried the drove alone once, as a pup. I got lost in an hour, and he found me by whistling.
  ask : Did anybody in your house ever find you by a sound like that?
  b : A voice across the market. I'd know it anywhere still.
  b[from=larkfield] : The drove roads take some learning. Everybody gets lost once.

rule @walk_on
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Walk on, now. Walk on. | Steady, the pair of you. #oath#.

rule @halfrain_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=rain self.dislikes=drizzle
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #halfrain.capitalize#. Make your mind up. | Ropes slack again. #annoyed#.

rule @stone_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter here.time=dawn|day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Good day to you, old stone. | Still standing, #leaner#? Good.

rule @birds_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #roofbirds.capitalize# are in. Day's done. | There's the big one on the chimney again.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. I've a minute.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Need something carried? | #topic.player#. #talk_open#
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I'm just in off the road. Be quick, if you can.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=carter] : I drive for the carters. Out at dawn, back after the lamps, a load each way. | I drive #cart# out of #self.workplace# and back. I'm learning the hills.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work, and I keep #maps#. That's me. | #job_busy# Mostly on the road.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# I'm on the road all day. | Nothing that reached #hillroad#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.news] : They were saying at the yard: from #world.news_from#, #world.news#. | Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. That's all I know.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Not #load# to carry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the ruts.
graft resident.hub
choice Do you really talk to the milestones? -> stones
node stones
say Only good day. They've stood by the road two hundred years and watched every cart go by. It seems rude not to.
mood calm
free
choice Do they ever answer? -> stones_answer
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node stones_answer
say No. That's what I like about them. But on a bad road, in the fog, it helps to know there's an old friend every mile.
choice Something else. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
